        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({\n  contents: [{ parts: [{ text: [\n    'You are a short-form video scriptwriter. Write an English narration script about: ' + $json.topic + '.',\n    'Tone: ' + $json.tone + '. Use exactly ' + $json.scene_count + ' scenes, about 40 seconds in total.',\n    'Rules:',\n    '- Scene 1 is the hook: a surprising fact, bold claim or question in under 12 words. Never start with \"Today\" or \"In this video\".',\n    '- Each scene is 1-2 short sentences, 12-22 words, written to be spoken aloud in plain conversational words.',\n    '- One idea per scene, and each scene makes the viewer curious about the next one.',\n    '- The last scene gives a memorable takeaway and a short call to action.',\n    '- No filler, no jargon, and no facts you are not sure about.',\n    '- on_screen_text: max 5 punchy words.',\n    '- image_prompt: one clear visual with subject, action, setting and mood, matching character_description. Do not mention an art style and do not put text in the image.',\n    'Return JSON only in this shape: {\"title\": \"catchy title\", \"character_description\": \"one sentence describing the main character or visual motif for consistent images\", \"scenes\": [{\"script\": \"narration\", \"image_prompt\": \"visual description\", \"on_screen_text\": \"short caption\"}]}'\n  ].join('\\n') }] }],\n  generationConfig: { responseMimeType: \"application/json\" }\n}) }}",
        "options": {}
